'''Taunt''' is a [[debuff]] that makes an affected enemy unable to consider any object as a potential target, except the source of the debuff. It also causes enemies to deal 10% less [[damage]] to other entities.<ref name="MechanicalQuestionsThread2.3.0" /><ref name="DevManifesto2.3.0" /> It lasts for 3 seconds. Taunt can be applied by players, minions, monsters, or [[proxies]] that are targetable (e.g. [[totem]]s, but not [[trap]]s, [[mine]]s, or [[Mirage (proxy)|mirage]]s). Taunt immediately expires when the character (or proxy) that applied it dies or expires. 

When multiple sources are taunting the same enemy, the first taunt applied determines the aggro. The targeted source can maintain aggro indefinitely as long as it maintains its taunt on the target.<ref name="DevManifesto2.3.0"/>

All targets can be taunted unless made immune through a modifier; however, taunt will not cause [[The Shaper]], [[The Elder]], [[Guardian of the Void|Shaper Guardians]], [[Elder Guardians]], or various other unique bosses to retarget towards the source of the taunt.<ref name="patch3.2.0notes"/>

